.TH SNOWTRIX 1 "snowtrix" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snowtrix \- interactive snowfall simulation for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snowtrix
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snowtrix
is an interactive terminal-based particle engine that simulates
falling snow, wind, snow accumulation, and mouse interaction.

Snowflakes are rendered using multiple depth layers to create a
simple parallax effect. The simulation can be modified interactively
while it is running.

.B snowtrix
is written in C99 and uses termbox2 for terminal interaction.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -a
Enable snow accumulation when the program starts.
.TP
.B -p
Start the program directly in Party Mode.
.TP
.BI "-c " RRGGBB
Set the foreground snow color.
.TP
.BI "-m " RRGGBB
Set the middle-layer snow color.
.TP
.BI "-f " RRGGBB
Set the background-layer snow color.
.TP
.BI "-C " theme
Select a predefined color theme.
.TP
.BI "-s " speed
Set the initial falling speed.
.TP
.BI "-w " wind
Set the initial wind force.
.TP
.BI "-b " flakes
Set the number of active snowflakes.
.TP
.B "-h, --help"
Display a help message and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
.SS General
.TP
.B q
Quit the program.
.TP
.B ESC
Quit the program.
.TP
.B a
Toggle snow accumulation.
.TP
.B s
Toggle Spring Mode, which automatically melts accumulated snow.
.TP
.B p
Toggle Party Mode.
.SS Environment
.TP
.B >, .
Increase wind force to the right.
.TP
.B <, ,
Increase wind force to the left.
.TP
.B w
Calm the wind.
.TP
.B +, =
Increase falling speed.
.TP
.B -, _
Decrease falling speed.
.TP
.B m
Add 50 active snowflakes.
.TP
.B l
Remove 50 active snowflakes.
.SS COLOR PRESETS
.TP
.B !
Red.
.TP
.B @
Green.
.TP
.B #
Yellow.
.TP
.B $
Blue.
.TP
.B %
Magenta.
.TP
.B ^
Cyan.
.TP
.B &
White.
.TP
.B )
Dark gray.
.SH MOUSE
Mouse interaction can be used to influence snowflakes and accumulated
snow. Moving or clicking the mouse can push snowflakes around and
dig into accumulated snow.

Mouse support depends on the terminal emulator providing mouse
tracking.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B Accumulation
Allows snow to build up on the ground and spread across the surface.
.TP
.B Spring Mode
Dynamically melts accumulated snow while the simulation continues.
.TP
.B Party Mode
Replaces normal snow colors with animated RGB colors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B snowtrix
does not require a special environment configuration.

It requires a Linux or other POSIX-compatible system with a terminal
capable of providing the functionality required by termbox2.
.SH FILES
No configuration files are required by
.B snowtrix.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The program terminated successfully.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred.
.SH NOTES
.B snowtrix
is a terminal application. Its appearance and some interactive
behavior may vary between terminal emulators.

Resizing the terminal while the simulation is running may produce
minor visual artifacts during redraw.

Snowflake glyphs may appear differently depending on the terminal's
font and Unicode support.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the simulation normally:
.PP
.nf
.RS
snowtrix
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start with accumulated snow enabled:
.PP
.nf
.RS
snowtrix -a
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start in Party Mode:
.PP
.nf
.RS
snowtrix -p
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start with a custom foreground color:
.PP
.nf
.RS
snowtrix -c ff0000
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start with a custom speed, wind, and snowflake count:
.PP
.nf
.RS
snowtrix -s 2 -w 1 -b 500
.RE
.fi
.SH BUGS
Known limitations include visual artifacts when resizing the terminal
during execution, terminal-dependent mouse support, and differences
in Unicode snowflake rendering between terminal fonts.

Bug reports and patches should be submitted through the project's
repository.
